  takeaways: [
    'Q3 2026 beat on profit: non-GAAP EPS US$0.48 vs ~US$0.45 Street; revenue US$28.05bn was flat YoY and a touch below Tesla’s own US$28.34bn compiled consensus.',
    'Margins recovered: GAAP gross margin 19.6% (Q2 16.8%), auto margin ex-credits 18.1% (Q2 16.3%), energy margin 33.1% helped by tariff refunds and a vendor warranty true-down. Operating margin is still thin at 2.6% as R&D rose to US$2.76bn.',
    'Cash turned positive again: free cash flow +US$1.53bn after −US$1.09bn in Q2; capex US$4.73bn; 2026 capex guidance cut to about US$20bn; cash and investments US$45.4bn.',
    'Autonomy is ramping: 1.74m active FSD subscriptions (+67% YoY), >75% North America paid attach at delivery, nearly 2m cumulative unsupervised Robotaxi miles, Dallas Cybercab launch due next month.',
    'Regulatory credits are fading (US$113m vs US$417m a year ago); regulators remain the swing factor for FSD in the EU (Musk: by Q1 2027) and China (still no approval).',
    'Optimus early production has started in Fremont, but Musk guided to at least a year to reach 20,000 a week and outside customers around end-2027; the SpaceX merger review adds a new overhang/catalyst.'],
